<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Triangle PQR, with <m>P({-2},\,{-1})</m>, <m>Q({4},\,{2})</m> and <m>R({2},\,{-3})</m>, is mapped onto triangle <m>P'Q'R'</m>, with <m>P'({-4},\,{-1})</m>, <m>Q'({8},\,{2})</m> and <m>R'({4},\,{-3})</m>, by a stretch.</p><p>(a) Which axis is invariant?</p><div>[ neither axis | the x-axis | the y-axis ]  </div><p>(b) The stretch factor is</p><div><fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) The matrix of the stretch is</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Every y-coordinate stays the same and every x-coordinate changes, so the points move parallel to the x-axis, at right angles to the y-axis. The y-axis is invariant.</p><p>(b) Stretch factor = new distance from the invariant axis <m>\div</m> old distance. For P: <m>{4} \div {2} = {2}</m>.</p><p>(c) The images of (1, 0) and (0, 1) are the columns: <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 2 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>the y-axis</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left[\begin{array}{cc} 2 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>